From 3c82e42ed1fd0c05bd794e78c69ec3216f04a9bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bemly <bemly_@petalmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 12:57:53 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Sinytra patch 0009: make child-process services bindable
 cross-package

The Gecko child services (tab/gpu/socket/...) ship in the webview
provider package, but GeckoProcessManager/ServiceUtils resolved them
against the host app package: intents targeted a package without the
services (NameNotFoundException) and the services themselves were
exported=false (bind denied). Either failure leaves XRE without children
(native SEGV in the launcher thread on spawn failure).

- ServiceUtils.getComponentPackage: resolves the package that actually
  carries the GeckoView classes (classloader mozglue path, verified
  against WebView.getCurrentWebViewPackage sourceDir), cached; regular
  embedders hit the context-APK fast path unchanged.
- DefaultBindDelegate/IsolatedBindDelegate + getServiceFlags/
  getServiceList use it for ComponentName/Intent/package lookups.
- Child services exported=true in the overlay manifest so another app
  may bind them.
